    "# Poker Bankroll Risk Model\n",
    "### Monte Carlo simulation of risk of ruin, drawdowns and capital sizing\n",
    "\n",
    "**The question:** a poker player has a real edge, but results swing hard from session to session. How much capital do they need so that bad luck doesn't wipe them out before the edge pays off?\n",
    "\n",
    "This is the same problem a trader, a fund or a startup faces: a positive expected return, high volatility, and a capital base that can hit zero first. The model below:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. Simulates 10,000 possible 10,000-hand futures for one player\n",
    "2. Measures risk of ruin, drawdowns and the spread of outcomes\n",
    "3. Checks the simulation against the closed-form math to confirm it's right\n",
    "4. Tests how many simulations are needed for a stable answer\n",
    "5. Maps how bankroll size and skill trade off against risk\n",
    "\n",
    "A companion Excel version of this model (500 paths, formula-driven, with a dashboard) lives alongside this notebook."
   ]
