    "## 1. Assumptions\n",
    "\n",
    "Defaults describe a winning $1/$2 No-Limit Hold'em cash player. Results are simulated in **blocks of 100 hands**, the unit poker players use for win rate and standard deviation.\n",
    "\n",
    "| Input | Value | Why |\n",
    "|---|---|---|\n",
    "| Win rate | 5 big blinds / 100 hands | A solid low-stakes winner |\n",
    "| Standard deviation | 90 big blinds / 100 hands | Typical NLHE cash games run roughly 80–100 |\n",
    "| Bankroll | $2,000 (10 buy-ins) | A common but aggressive bankroll |"
   ]
  },
