    "## 4. Check the simulation against the math\n",
    "\n",
    "A simulation is only useful if it's right. Bankroll over time behaves like a **random walk with drift**, which has known closed-form answers:\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Finite horizon** (going broke within *T* blocks), from the reflection principle:\n",
    "  $P = \\Phi\\left(\\frac{-B - \\mu T}{\\sigma\\sqrt{T}}\\right) + e^{-2\\mu B/\\sigma^2}\\,\\Phi\\left(\\frac{-B + \\mu T}{\\sigma\\sqrt{T}}\\right)$\n",
    "- **No time limit:** $P = e^{-2\\mu B/\\sigma^2}$\n",
    "\n",
    "where *B* is the bankroll, *μ* and *σ* are the mean and standard deviation per block, and Φ is the standard normal CDF.\n",
    "\n",
    "If the simulation matches these across a range of bankroll sizes, the code is doing what it should."
   ]
  },
