    "**Reading the check:** the simulated points sit on or just under the 10,000-hand theory line. The small, consistent gap is expected: the simulation only checks the bankroll every 100 hands, so it misses dips to zero that happen *within* a block and then recover. The continuous formula counts those. This is called discretization bias, and it shrinks as blocks get smaller.\n",
